# Trivy ignore list for the zonic-postgresql-server-fastapi runtime image.
#
# Every entry here is an OS-level package that ships with the python:3.12-slim
# (Debian 13 "trixie") base image and is not exercised by this application at
# runtime (no perl, no gzip/ncurses/sqlite3/acl usage anywhere in this codebase).
# Each CVE below currently has no upstream Debian fix available (or Debian has
# explicitly deferred one) as of the scan that first surfaced it, 2026-08-26 —
# `docker build` + `apt-get upgrade` alone cannot resolve these; they're pinned
# here rather than left to fail every build until Debian ships a patch.
#
# Re-check this list periodically (e.g. when bumping the base image) and remove
# entries once a real fix lands — don't let it become a permanent blanket waiver.

# gzip — buffer overflow in LZH decompression, no fix available
CVE-2026-41992

# libacl1 — symlink traversal privilege escalation, no fix available
CVE-2026-54369

# ncurses (libncursesw6, libtinfo6, ncurses-base, ncurses-bin) — buffer overflow,
# no fix available
CVE-2025-69720

# libsqlite3-0 — arbitrary code execution / crash via crafted FTS5 data, no fix
# available
CVE-2026-11822
CVE-2026-11824

# perl-base and its bundled CPAN modules — none of this is invoked by this
# service (no perl scripts, no Archive::Tar/IO::Compress/Storable usage)
CVE-2026-13221
CVE-2026-8376
CVE-2026-42496
CVE-2026-42497
CVE-2026-48962
CVE-2026-57432
CVE-2026-57433
CVE-2026-9538
